.TH CARD 6.SH NAMEcard \- a Christmas card from Hanoi.SH SYNOPSIS\fBcard\fR.SH DESCRIPTIONThe Towers of Hanoi, played out on the screen, whose twelve disks are thelines of a Christmas greeting: as the tower is moved from peg to peg themessage comes apart and is built again.  It plays on, round and round,until you stop it with control-C.  By Istvan Mohos, 1984..PPIt moves the cursor through TERMCAP, so it wants TERM and TERMCAP set,and a terminal of at least 9600 baud to be worth watching..SH SEE ALSOhanoi, xmas